<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Daily Athlete Routine</title>

  <style>
    body {
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
      background-color: #eef5f9;
      color: #1c2d37;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      color: #0d47a1;
      margin-top: 25px;
    }

    /* Intro box matching size/borders */
    .intro {
      width: 800px;
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 15px;
      border: 2px solid #0d47a1;
      background-color: #ffffff;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    /* Side-by-side cards using float */
    .routine-card {
      width: 250px;
      height: 260px;
      float: left;
      margin: 15px;
      padding: 18px;
      border: 3px solid #0288d1;
      background-color: #ffffff;
      border-radius: 10px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }

    .routine-card h2 {
      color: #006064;
      font-size: 22px;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .routine-card p {
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #455a64;
    }

    .time {
      color: #c62828;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    /* Clears the floats so the next row drops down */
    .clear-section {
      clear: both;
    }

    /* Bottom Tip Box */
    .note {
      width: 800px;
      margin: 20px auto;
      padding: 15px;
      border: 2px dashed #ff8f00;
      background-color: #fff8e1;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1>Daily Athlete Routine</h1>

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      Welcome to my daily training schedule! This layout uses CSS float and box sizing to arrange fitness activity cards side-by-side.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Sunrise Warmup</h2>
    <p>
      Dynamic leg swings, arm circles, and light jogging to wake up muscles.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 12 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Agility Drills</h2>
    <p>
      Fast footwork, ladder runs, and cone shuttles for speed and reaction.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 18 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Core Circuit</h2>
    <p>
      Planks, russian twists, and bicycle crunches for abdominal strength.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 15 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="clear-section"></div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Core Hydro Blast</h2>
    <p>
      High-intensity swimming laps to boost lung capacity and endurance.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 30 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Cool Down Walk</h2>
    <p>
      Slow-paced treadmill walking combined with deep breathing techniques.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 20 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="routine-card">
    <h2>Foam Rolling</h2>
    <p>
      Target tight hamstring and back muscles to prevent soreness and injury.
    </p>
    <p class="time">Time: 10 minutes</p>
  </div>

  <div class="clear-section"></div>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      Pro Athlete Tip: Stay consistent, prioritize 8 hours of sleep, and always refuel with protein within 30 minutes post-workout!
    </p>
  </div>

</body>
</html>